This server edits one artifact in the user's Exhibit library, a personal library of small self-contained web tools. None of its tools takes an artifact id: every one acts on the single artifact the user's token was issued for, and the server refuses anything else.

{{template "artifact_format.tmpl"}}

Tools:
- get_artifact(): read the artifact's current source and metadata. Read before changing anything.
- edit_artifact(edits): targeted replacements, each {oldText, newText}. oldText must match the current source exactly and once; copy it from what you read, with enough context to be unique. Prefer this for anything short of a full rewrite.
- write_artifact(body[, title]): replace the whole source. Only for a genuine rewrite.
- get_state(), set_state(key, value), delete_state([key]): the artifact's stored state. delete_state with no key erases ALL of it, irreversibly; only when the user clearly asked for that.
- get_widget(), set_widget(body), edit_widget(edits): the artifact's gallery widget, described below.

Every save carries the revision you last read. If the artifact or widget changed since (someone edited it in the browser, say), the save is refused and nothing is written: read it again, reapply your change to what is there now, and save again. Never write a body from memory to get past a refusal.

Saves are kept as versions the user can restore, labelled as made by an agent. The artifact's network allowlist and permissions are the user's to approve in Exhibit; a save reports origins the source references that are still blocked.

